and run Python with Astral UV. I'm just going to copy this. I'm going to open up a brand new terminal instance back into main.\n\nIf we open up programmable you'll see these three scripts and you'll also have the prompt that's going to run inside of every one of these scripts that's going to call clog code in a programmable fashion you can see here's the python version here's the shell version and here's the bun typescript version so before we kick this off let's go ahead clear up that branch and run git branch we can see that branch that was generated by the initial run i'm just going to get branch delete this and then i'm going to run the python version of this I'm gonna go ahead and kick this off and it's going to rerun that workflow. Here's the prompt it's running. And here is programmable.python.\n\nSo you can see this exactly what's running. If we open up.py, you can see exactly what this looks like. This is a key element, is a key advantage of Claude code that once again, differentiates it from all the other agentic coding tools. This is super, super critical, right? We need this capability of having a programmable agentic coding tool. Why is that? It's because we wanna be building systems that build systems for us. And with this, you can see these files are getting created, our branch just changed. With this capability, with the agentic coding tool that we can program, we can embed our own agents, our own workflows, our own agentic prompts across the software development lifecycle.\n\nThis is a critical distinguishing feature from Cloud Code. We need to be able to embed our tooling across the terminal, across developer environments to drive real engineering outcomes with and without our oversight. I hope this is all adding up. I hope your engineering mind is starting to turn at how important this capability is. It's not just about the agentic prompt. It's about where we can use the agentic prompt. and the fact that Cloud Code runs in the terminal, you can see there's our output there. In our prompt, we requested a full report of the outputs, and that's exactly what we got here.\n\nThe fact that Cloud Code runs in the terminal means we can run it across all developer environments, including full agentic environments where we're not even present. We're gonna be talking about agentic triggers in this course, but in addition to that, Cloud Code can be embedded inside of your code base firing off when it needs to doing the right thing at the right time. So these files got created, all of this work ran. Here's the prompt. You have access to all of this. This single code base, this hyper simple code base sets up and frames everything we're going to do in tactical agentic coding. We're going to take this idea of the agentic prompt and we're going to scale it to the max.\n\nGreat work here. This was a dense lesson one. But this essential tactic, stop coding, and the key difference between AI coding and agentic coding will ripple throughout every lesson moving forward. Agentic coding is not about us writing code. It's about building systems that build systems on our behalf. The contradicting truth about what you'll learn in tactical agentic coding is this. To become an irreplaceable engineer, you will replace yourself. You won't see any vibe coders replicating what you'll be able to do when you finish tactical agentic coding. Evolution is hard. It's challenging. We're going to push through hard concepts.\n\nOn lesson one, I've already requested that you stop coding, right? We're using the best tool for the job. Evolution forces us to leave skills behind to adapt new ones and bet on potential futures. But in the tech industry, this is where all the alpha lies. This is where your asymmetric engineering advantage exists. It's in the future. It's in pushing what's possible forward. Let's start scaling the core for the Identic Prompt and Cloud Code into real engineering work across worlds. the software development lifecycle. Next up, we'll explore the most important leverage points of agentic coding so that 10 minutes of your work is equivalent to 60 minutes or more of another engineer's work.\n\nGreat job here. I'll see you in lesson two.\n","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}}},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CcxHwaCZfKkxM95hXEUsE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DN5vwRXyCUyBPrV1UqaM8G","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kvnkishore/WebstormProjects/AgenticEngineer/IndyDevDan/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding/transcript/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding-notes.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5417,"cache_read_input_tokens":42433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5417},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a","uuid":"65a628b4-005f-4719-a8f1-93f26ff7bc53","request_id":"req_011CcxHwY5p1YaAvpniQPaxx"},{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DN5vwRXyCUyBPrV1UqaM8G","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Hello Agentic Coding - Become the Engineer They Can't Replace\n2\t**Lesson #1 (Beginner)**  ·  https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding/course/hello-agentic-coding\n3\t\n4\t_Discover why your hands and mind are no longer the best tools for writing code. Make the hard, but important decision to let go of the old ways of engineering to adopt the new. Set the stage for learning the new way to engineering with agents and the core four._\n5\t\n6\t## Loot Box — 28 notes\n7\t\n8\t### 🔥 AI Coding is NOT enough\n9\tAI coding is NOT enough. Engineering is about much more than just writing code. AI coding was just phase one. Agentic coding marks phase two - this is where real engineers strike back.\n10\t\n11\t### 🔥 TAC Mission: Become Irreplaceable\n12\tWe have one mission in tactical agentic coding: transform you into an engineer they can't replace. You know who they are. It's your boss. It's the company. It's the industry. It's AI.\n13\t\n14\t### 🔥 Commander of Compute\n15\tHow do we become irreplaceable? We move up the stack once again. We become a commander of compute. You don't just prompt to generate code. That's phase one engineering. You take this compute and use it to build systems that build systems.\n16\t\n17\t### 🔥 Engineering Was Never About Writing Code\n18\tEngineering was never about writing code. It's about building systems of leverage that produce valuable outcomes for your users and customers. Remember, you're an engineer, not a coder. The difference is massive.\n19\t\n20\t### 🔥 The 10X Engineer Opportunity\n21\tIn every software revolution, there's an opportunity for you to become the fabled 10X engineer, not by spending 10X the time or effort, but by achieving 10X leverage. The number is arbitrary - it's 2X, 10X, 100X. It all depends on the leverage points you can find.\n22\t\n23\t### 🔥 Transform Code Into Self-Operating Machines\n24\tThe irreplaceable engineer in phase two that we're aiming to become is the engineer that transforms their code bases into self-operating machines. You'll learn how to maximize your leverage so much so that your code base literally runs itself.\n25\t\n26\t### 🏆 Tactic #1: Stop Coding\n27\tYour hands and mind are no longer the best tool for the job of writing code. Language models wrapped in the right agent architecture, running on supercomputers are vastly superior coders than you and I are. Stop coding and use the best tool for the job.\n28\t\n29\t### 🔥 Throughout TAC: No Typing Code\n30\tThroughout TAC, Tactical Agentic Coding, we're not going to type a single line of code. This is the first and most foundational tactic. If you're still typing code, you have no chance of keeping up.\n31\t\n32\t### 🔥 Phase Two Role: Planning & Reviewing\n33\tTo scale into this new phase two role, we need to allocate our engineering cycles to planning, reviewing, and creating closed loop structures. Code understanding is still critically important, but we're not coding anymore.\n34\t\n35\t### ⚡ WSL (Windows Subsystem for Linux) Documentation\n36\tOfficial Microsoft documentation for WSL - run a Linux environment directly on Windows for development\n37\t\n38\t### ⚡ Vite Documentation\n39\tOfficial documentation for Vite - next generation frontend tooling with fast HMR and optimized build\n40\t\n41\t### ⚡ pytest Documentation\n42\tOfficial documentation for pytest - the Python testing framework for writing better programs\n43\t\n44\t### ⚡ npm Documentation\n45\tOfficial documentation for npm - the Node.js package manager and world's largest software registry\n46\t\n47\t### ⚡ Bun Documentation\n48\tOfficial documentation for Bun - all-in-one JavaScript runtime with built-in bundler, transpiler, and package manager\n49\t\n50\t### ⚡ Node.js Documentation\n51\tOfficial Node.js documentation - JavaScript runtime built on Chrome's V8 engine\n52\t\n53\t### ⚡ GitHub CLI Documentation\n54\tOfficial documentation for GitHub CLI (gh) - bring GitHub to your terminal for seamless workflow\n55\t\n56\t### ⚔️ TAC Lesson 1 - Hello Agentic Coding Repository\n57\tgit clone https://github.com/disler/tac-1.git\n58\t\n59\t### ⚡ Git Setup Guide\n60\tDownload and installation guide for Git version control\n61\t\n62\t### ⚡ UV (Astral) Setup Guide\n63\tInstallation and setup guide for UV, the fast Python package manager\n64\t\n65\t### ⚡ Python Setup Guide\n66\tInstallation and setup guide for Python\n67\t\n68\t### ⚡ Claude Code Setup Guide\n69\tGet started with Claude Code for agentic coding\n70\t\n71\t### 📜 Claude Code: Primary Agentic Tool\n72\tThroughout tactical agentic coding, Claude Code will be our primary agentic coding tool. We're going to be using millions and millions of tokens. Just as Aider was for the AI coding phase one era, Claude Code represents the best phase two agentic coding tool.\n73\t\n74\t### 🔥 The Core Four: Context, Model, Prompt, Tools\n75\tAgentic coding expands the big three (context, model, prompt) by adding tools. When you add reliable tool execution, we upgrade the big three to the core four: context, model, prompt, and tools.\n76\t\n77\t### 🔥 Long-Running AI Developer Workflows\n78\tWhen you take the core four and wrap it in an agentic coding tool like Claude Code, you can create long running end-to-end AI developer workflows that run for minutes to hours with and without your oversight.\n79\t\n80\t### 🔥 Programmable Agentic Coding\n81\tClaude Code is programmable - you can run it from any programming language that has terminal access. We can embed our own agents, workflows, and agentic prompts across the software development lifecycle.\n82\t\n83\t### 🔥 Building Systems That Build Systems\n84\tWe need this capability of having a programmable agentic coding tool because we want to be building systems that build systems for us. We can embed our tooling across developer environments to drive real engineering outcomes.\n85\t\n86\t### 🔥 Lesson 1 Foundation Complete\n87\tThis essential tactic, stop coding, and the key difference between AI coding and agentic coding will ripple throughout every lesson moving forward. Agentic coding is about building systems that build systems on our behalf.\n88\t\n89\t### 🔥 To Become Irreplaceable, Replace Yourself\n90\tThe contradicting truth about what you'll learn in tactical agentic coding: To become an irreplaceable engineer, you will replace yourself. You won't see any vibe coders replicating what you'll be able to do. Agentic Engineer Master AI Coding, AI Agents, and Agentics to build 'living' software Blogs Pi Coding Agent: The Only Claude Code Competitor Top 2% Agentic Engineering The Agent Thread Framework State of AI Coding Compute Advantage Resources Home Account Tactical Agentic Coding Principled AI Coding YouTube Terms Privacy\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a","uuid":"63d82f47-1535-4b00-9896-7c95de38d500","timestamp":"2026-07-12T14:07:04.565Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kvnkishore/WebstormProjects/AgenticEngineer/IndyDevDan/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding/transcript/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding-notes.md","content":"# Hello Agentic Coding - Become the Engineer They Can't Replace\n**Lesson #1 (Beginner)**  ·  https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding/course/hello-agentic-coding\n\n_Discover why your hands and mind are no longer the best tools for writing code. Make the hard, but important decision to let go of the old ways of engineering to adopt the new. Set the stage for learning the new way to engineering with agents and the core four._\n\n## Loot Box — 28 notes\n\n### 🔥 AI Coding is NOT enough\nAI coding is NOT enough. Engineering is about much more than just writing code. AI coding was just phase one. Agentic coding marks phase two - this is where real engineers strike back.\n\n### 🔥 TAC Mission: Become Irreplaceable\nWe have one mission in tactical agentic coding: transform you into an engineer they can't replace. You know who they are. It's your boss. It's the company. It's the industry. It's AI.\n\n### 🔥 Commander of Compute\nHow do we become irreplaceable? We move up the stack once again. We become a commander of compute. You don't just prompt to generate code. That's phase one engineering. You take this compute and use it to build systems that build systems.\n\n### 🔥 Engineering Was Never About Writing Code\nEngineering was never about writing code. It's about building systems of leverage that produce valuable outcomes for your users and customers. Remember, you're an engineer, not a coder. The difference is massive.\n\n### 🔥 The 10X Engineer Opportunity\nIn every software revolution, there's an opportunity for you to become the fabled 10X engineer, not by spending 10X the time or effort, but by achieving 10X leverage. The number is arbitrary - it's 2X, 10X, 100X. It all depends on the leverage points you can find.\n\n### 🔥 Transform Code Into Self-Operating Machines\nThe irreplaceable engineer in phase two that we're aiming to become is the engineer that transforms their code bases into self-operating machines. You'll learn how to maximize your leverage so much so that your code base literally runs itself.\n\n### 🏆 Tactic #1: Stop Coding\nYour hands and mind are no longer the best tool for the job of writing code. Language models wrapped in the right agent architecture, running on supercomputers are vastly superior coders than you and I are. Stop coding and use the best tool for the job.\n\n### 🔥 Throughout TAC: No Typing Code\nThroughout TAC, Tactical Agentic Coding, we're not going to type a single line of code. This is the first and most foundational tactic. If you're still typing code, you have no chance of keeping up.\n\n### 🔥 Phase Two Role: Planning & Reviewing\nTo scale into this new phase two role, we need to allocate our engineering cycles to planning, reviewing, and creating closed loop structures. Code understanding is still critically important, but we're not coding anymore.\n\n### ⚡ WSL (Windows Subsystem for Linux) Documentation\nOfficial Microsoft documentation for WSL - run a Linux environment directly on Windows for development\n\n### ⚡ Vite Documentation\nOfficial documentation for Vite - next generation frontend tooling with fast HMR and optimized build\n\n### ⚡ pytest Documentation\nOfficial documentation for pytest - the Python testing framework for writing better programs\n\n### ⚡ npm Documentation\nOfficial documentation for npm - the Node.js package manager and world's largest software registry\n\n### ⚡ Bun Documentation\nOfficial documentation for Bun - all-in-one JavaScript runtime with built-in bundler, transpiler, and package manager\n\n### ⚡ Node.js Documentation\nOfficial Node.js documentation - JavaScript runtime built on Chrome's V8 engine\n\n### ⚡ GitHub CLI Documentation\nOfficial documentation for GitHub CLI (gh) - bring GitHub to your terminal for seamless workflow\n\n### ⚔️ TAC Lesson 1 - Hello Agentic Coding Repository\ngit clone https://github.com/disler/tac-1.git\n\n### ⚡ Git Setup Guide\nDownload and installation guide for Git version control\n\n### ⚡ UV (Astral) Setup Guide\nInstallation and setup guide for UV, the fast Python package manager\n\n### ⚡ Python Setup Guide\nInstallation and setup guide for Python\n\n### ⚡ Claude Code Setup Guide\nGet started with Claude Code for agentic coding\n\n### 📜 Claude Code: Primary Agentic Tool\nThroughout tactical agentic coding, Claude Code will be our primary agentic coding tool. We're going to be using millions and millions of tokens. Just as Aider was for the AI coding phase one era, Claude Code represents the best phase two agentic coding tool.\n\n### 🔥 The Core Four: Context, Model, Prompt, Tools\nAgentic coding expands the big three (context, model, prompt) by adding tools. When you add reliable tool execution, we upgrade the big three to the core four: context, model, prompt, and tools.\n\n### 🔥 Long-Running AI Developer Workflows\nWhen you take the core four and wrap it in an agentic coding tool like Claude Code, you can create long running end-to-end AI developer workflows that run for minutes to hours with and without your oversight.\n\n### 🔥 Programmable Agentic Coding\nClaude Code is programmable - you can run it from any programming language that has terminal access. We can embed our own agents, workflows, and agentic prompts across the software development lifecycle.\n\n### 🔥 Building Systems That Build Systems\nWe need this capability of having a programmable agentic coding tool because we want to be building systems that build systems for us. We can embed our tooling across developer environments to drive real engineering outcomes.\n\n### 🔥 Lesson 1 Foundation Complete\nThis essential tactic, stop coding, and the key difference between AI coding and agentic coding will ripple throughout every lesson moving forward. Agentic coding is about building systems that build systems on our behalf.\n\n### 🔥 To Become Irreplaceable, Replace Yourself\nThe contradicting truth about what you'll learn in tactical agentic coding: To become an irreplaceable engineer, you will replace yourself. You won't see any vibe coders replicating what you'll be able to do. Agentic Engineer Master AI Coding, AI Agents, and Agentics to build 'living' software Blogs Pi Coding Agent: The Only Claude Code Competitor Top 2% Agentic Engineering The Agent Thread Framework State of AI Coding Compute Advantage Resources Home Account Tactical Agentic Coding Principled AI Coding YouTube Terms Privacy\n","numLines":91,"startLine":1,"totalLines":91}}},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CcxHwaCZfKkxM95hXEUsE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WvPUiKLwFhnTD4SFmhGiNt","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kvnkishore/WebstormProjects/AgenticEngineer/IndyDevDan/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding/metadata/lesson.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5417,"cache_read_input_tokens":42433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5417},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a","uuid":"05e626ff-bf41-40a6-a2c6-193c95b89285","request_id":"req_011CcxHwY5p1YaAvpniQPaxx"},{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WvPUiKLwFhnTD4SFmhGiNt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"key\": \"tac-1-hello-agentic-coding\",\n3\t  \"short_key\": \"tac-1\",\n4\t  \"title\": \"Hello Agentic Coding\",\n5\t  \"course\": \"TAC\",\n6\t  \"slug\": \"hello-agentic-coding\",\n7\t  \"url\": \"https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding/course/hello-agentic-coding\",\n8\t  \"order\": 1,\n9\t  \"video_file\": \"tac-1-hello-agentic-coding.mp4\",\n10\t  \"codebase\": \"tac/tac-1\",\n11\t  \"course_page_html\": \"course-page.html\",\n12\t  \"course_page_source\": \"agenticengineer.com outerHTML + local Nuxt CSS/fonts/images (offline)\",\n13\t  \"course_page_bytes\": 35734,\n14\t  \"course_page_offline\": true,\n15\t  \"course_notes\": \"course-notes.md\"\n16\t}\n17\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a","uuid":"aece642e-802d-42fd-acaf-849035c091a2","timestamp":"2026-07-12T14:07:05.485Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kvnkishore/WebstormProjects/AgenticEngineer/IndyDevDan/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding/metadata/lesson.json","content":"{\n  \"key\": \"tac-1-hello-agentic-coding\",\n  \"short_key\": \"tac-1\",\n  \"title\": \"Hello Agentic Coding\",\n  \"course\": \"TAC\",\n  \"slug\": \"hello-agentic-coding\",\n  \"url\": \"https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding/course/hello-agentic-coding\",\n  \"order\": 1,\n  \"video_file\": \"tac-1-hello-agentic-coding.mp4\",\n  \"codebase\": \"tac/tac-1\",\n  \"course_page_html\": \"course-page.html\",\n  \"course_page_source\": \"agenticengineer.com outerHTML + local Nuxt CSS/fonts/images (offline)\",\n  \"course_page_bytes\": 35734,\n  \"course_page_offline\": true,\n  \"course_notes\": \"course-notes.md\"\n}\n","numLines":17,"startLine":1,"totalLines":17}}},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CcxHwaCZfKkxM95hXEUsE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017t7uCPW5wP957oxDrQCjuW","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kvnkishore/WebstormProjects/AgenticEngineer/IndyDevDan/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding/metadata/course-notes.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5417,"cache_read_input_tokens":42433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5417},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a","uuid":"f5ce94ad-2970-4ff7-91d1-bbf924a7ece4","request_id":"req_011CcxHwY5p1YaAvpniQPaxx"},{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017t7uCPW5wP957oxDrQCjuW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Hello Agentic Coding - Become the Engineer They Can't Replace\n2\t**Lesson #1 (Beginner)**  ·  https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding/course/hello-agentic-coding\n3\t\n4\t_Discover why your hands and mind are no longer the best tools for writing code. Make the hard, but important decision to let go of the old ways of engineering to adopt the new. Set the stage for learning the new way to engineering with agents and the core four._\n5\t\n6\t## Loot Box — 28 notes\n7\t\n8\t### 🔥 AI Coding is NOT enough\n9\tAI coding is NOT enough. Engineering is about much more than just writing code. AI coding was just phase one. Agentic coding marks phase two - this is where real engineers strike back.\n10\t\n11\t### 🔥 TAC Mission: Become Irreplaceable\n12\tWe have one mission in tactical agentic coding: transform you into an engineer they can't replace. You know who they are. It's your boss. It's the company. It's the industry. It's AI.\n13\t\n14\t### 🔥 Commander of Compute\n15\tHow do we become irreplaceable? We move up the stack once again. We become a commander of compute. You don't just prompt to generate code. That's phase one engineering. You take this compute and use it to build systems that build systems.\n16\t\n17\t### 🔥 Engineering Was Never About Writing Code\n18\tEngineering was never about writing code. It's about building systems of leverage that produce valuable outcomes for your users and customers. Remember, you're an engineer, not a coder. The difference is massive.\n19\t\n20\t### 🔥 The 10X Engineer Opportunity\n21\tIn every software revolution, there's an opportunity for you to become the fabled 10X engineer, not by spending 10X the time or effort, but by achieving 10X leverage. The number is arbitrary - it's 2X, 10X, 100X. It all depends on the leverage points you can find.\n22\t\n23\t### 🔥 Transform Code Into Self-Operating Machines\n24\tThe irreplaceable engineer in phase two that we're aiming to become is the engineer that transforms their code bases into self-operating machines. You'll learn how to maximize your leverage so much so that your code base literally runs itself.\n25\t\n26\t### 🏆 Tactic #1: Stop Coding\n27\tYour hands and mind are no longer the best tool for the job of writing code. Language models wrapped in the right agent architecture, running on supercomputers are vastly superior coders than you and I are. Stop coding and use the best tool for the job.\n28\t\n29\t### 🔥 Throughout TAC: No Typing Code\n30\tThroughout TAC, Tactical Agentic Coding, we're not going to type a single line of code. This is the first and most foundational tactic. If you're still typing code, you have no chance of keeping up.\n31\t\n32\t### 🔥 Phase Two Role: Planning & Reviewing\n33\tTo scale into this new phase two role, we need to allocate our engineering cycles to planning, reviewing, and creating closed loop structures. Code understanding is still critically important, but we're not coding anymore.\n34\t\n35\t### ⚡ WSL (Windows Subsystem for Linux) Documentation\n36\tOfficial Microsoft documentation for WSL - run a Linux environment directly on Windows for development\n37\t\n38\t### ⚡ Vite Documentation\n39\tOfficial documentation for Vite - next generation frontend tooling with fast HMR and optimized build\n40\t\n41\t### ⚡ pytest Documentation\n42\tOfficial documentation for pytest - the Python testing framework for writing better programs\n43\t\n44\t### ⚡ npm Documentation\n45\tOfficial documentation for npm - the Node.js package manager and world's largest software registry\n46\t\n47\t### ⚡ Bun Documentation\n48\tOfficial documentation for Bun - all-in-one JavaScript runtime with built-in bundler, transpiler, and package manager\n49\t\n50\t### ⚡ Node.js Documentation\n51\tOfficial Node.js documentation - JavaScript runtime built on Chrome's V8 engine\n52\t\n53\t### ⚡ GitHub CLI Documentation\n54\tOfficial documentation for GitHub CLI (gh) - bring GitHub to your terminal for seamless workflow\n55\t\n56\t### ⚔️ TAC Lesson 1 - Hello Agentic Coding Repository\n57\tgit clone https://github.com/disler/tac-1.git\n58\t\n59\t### ⚡ Git Setup Guide\n60\tDownload and installation guide for Git version control\n61\t\n62\t### ⚡ UV (Astral) Setup Guide\n63\tInstallation and setup guide for UV, the fast Python package manager\n64\t\n65\t### ⚡ Python Setup Guide\n66\tInstallation and setup guide for Python\n67\t\n68\t### ⚡ Claude Code Setup Guide\n69\tGet started with Claude Code for agentic coding\n70\t\n71\t### 📜 Claude Code: Primary Agentic Tool\n72\tThroughout tactical agentic coding, Claude Code will be our primary agentic coding tool. We're going to be using millions and millions of tokens. Just as Aider was for the AI coding phase one era, Claude Code represents the best phase two agentic coding tool.\n73\t\n74\t### 🔥 The Core Four: Context, Model, Prompt, Tools\n75\tAgentic coding expands the big three (context, model, prompt) by adding tools. When you add reliable tool execution, we upgrade the big three to the core four: context, model, prompt, and tools.\n76\t\n77\t### 🔥 Long-Running AI Developer Workflows\n78\tWhen you take the core four and wrap it in an agentic coding tool like Claude Code, you can create long running end-to-end AI developer workflows that run for minutes to hours with and without your oversight.\n79\t\n80\t### 🔥 Programmable Agentic Coding\n81\tClaude Code is programmable - you can run it from any programming language that has terminal access. We can embed our own agents, workflows, and agentic prompts across the software development lifecycle.\n82\t\n83\t### 🔥 Building Systems That Build Systems\n84\tWe need this capability of having a programmable agentic coding tool because we want to be building systems that build systems for us. We can embed our tooling across developer environments to drive real engineering outcomes.\n85\t\n86\t### 🔥 Lesson 1 Foundation Complete\n87\tThis essential tactic, stop coding, and the key difference between AI coding and agentic coding will ripple throughout every lesson moving forward. Agentic coding is about building systems that build systems on our behalf.\n88\t\n89\t### 🔥 To Become Irreplaceable, Replace Yourself\n90\tThe contradicting truth about what you'll learn in tactical agentic coding: To become an irreplaceable engineer, you will replace yourself. You won't see any vibe coders replicating what you'll be able to do. Agentic Engineer Master AI Coding, AI Agents, and Agentics to build 'living' software Blogs Pi Coding Agent: The Only Claude Code Competitor Top 2% Agentic Engineering The Agent Thread Framework State of AI Coding Compute Advantage Resources Home Account Tactical Agentic Coding Principled AI Coding YouTube Terms Privacy\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a","uuid":"9794d741-ca3f-41e2-8a1b-38a9568ea044","timestamp":"2026-07-12T14:07:06.488Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kvnkishore/WebstormProjects/AgenticEngineer/IndyDevDan/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding/metadata/course-notes.md","content":"# Hello Agentic Coding - Become the Engineer They Can't Replace\n**Lesson #1 (Beginner)**  ·  https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding/course/hello-agentic-coding\n\n_Discover why your hands and mind are no longer the best tools for writing code. Make the hard, but important decision to let go of the old ways of engineering to adopt the new. Set the stage for learning the new way to engineering with agents and the core four._\n\n## Loot Box — 28 notes\n\n### 🔥 AI Coding is NOT enough\nAI coding is NOT enough. Engineering is about much more than just writing code. AI coding was just phase one. Agentic coding marks phase two - this is where real engineers strike back.\n\n### 🔥 TAC Mission: Become Irreplaceable\nWe have one mission in tactical agentic coding: transform you into an engineer they can't replace. You know who they are. It's your boss. It's the company. It's the industry. It's AI.\n\n### 🔥 Commander of Compute\nHow do we become irreplaceable? We move up the stack once again. We become a commander of compute. You don't just prompt to generate code. That's phase one engineering. You take this compute and use it to build systems that build systems.\n\n### 🔥 Engineering Was Never About Writing Code\nEngineering was never about writing code. It's about building systems of leverage that produce valuable outcomes for your users and customers. Remember, you're an engineer, not a coder. The difference is massive.\n\n### 🔥 The 10X Engineer Opportunity\nIn every software revolution, there's an opportunity for you to become the fabled 10X engineer, not by spending 10X the time or effort, but by achieving 10X leverage. The number is arbitrary - it's 2X, 10X, 100X. It all depends on the leverage points you can find.\n\n### 🔥 Transform Code Into Self-Operating Machines\nThe irreplaceable engineer in phase two that we're aiming to become is the engineer that transforms their code bases into self-operating machines. You'll learn how to maximize your leverage so much so that your code base literally runs itself.\n\n### 🏆 Tactic #1: Stop Coding\nYour hands and mind are no longer the best tool for the job of writing code. Language models wrapped in the right agent architecture, running on supercomputers are vastly superior coders than you and I are. Stop coding and use the best tool for the job.\n\n### 🔥 Throughout TAC: No Typing Code\nThroughout TAC, Tactical Agentic Coding, we're not going to type a single line of code. This is the first and most foundational tactic. If you're still typing code, you have no chance of keeping up.\n\n### 🔥 Phase Two Role: Planning & Reviewing\nTo scale into this new phase two role, we need to allocate our engineering cycles to planning, reviewing, and creating closed loop structures. Code understanding is still critically important, but we're not coding anymore.\n\n### ⚡ WSL (Windows Subsystem for Linux) Documentation\nOfficial Microsoft documentation for WSL - run a Linux environment directly on Windows for development\n\n### ⚡ Vite Documentation\nOfficial documentation for Vite - next generation frontend tooling with fast HMR and optimized build\n\n### ⚡ pytest Documentation\nOfficial documentation for pytest - the Python testing framework for writing better programs\n\n### ⚡ npm Documentation\nOfficial documentation for npm - the Node.js package manager and world's largest software registry\n\n### ⚡ Bun Documentation\nOfficial documentation for Bun - all-in-one JavaScript runtime with built-in bundler, transpiler, and package manager\n\n### ⚡ Node.js Documentation\nOfficial Node.js documentation - JavaScript runtime built on Chrome's V8 engine\n\n### ⚡ GitHub CLI Documentation\nOfficial documentation for GitHub CLI (gh) - bring GitHub to your terminal for seamless workflow\n\n### ⚔️ TAC Lesson 1 - Hello Agentic Coding Repository\ngit clone https://github.com/disler/tac-1.git\n\n### ⚡ Git Setup Guide\nDownload and installation guide for Git version control\n\n### ⚡ UV (Astral) Setup Guide\nInstallation and setup guide for UV, the fast Python package manager\n\n### ⚡ Python Setup Guide\nInstallation and setup guide for Python\n\n### ⚡ Claude Code Setup Guide\nGet started with Claude Code for agentic coding\n\n### 📜 Claude Code: Primary Agentic Tool\nThroughout tactical agentic coding, Claude Code will be our primary agentic coding tool. We're going to be using millions and millions of tokens. Just as Aider was for the AI coding phase one era, Claude Code represents the best phase two agentic coding tool.\n\n### 🔥 The Core Four: Context, Model, Prompt, Tools\nAgentic coding expands the big three (context, model, prompt) by adding tools. When you add reliable tool execution, we upgrade the big three to the core four: context, model, prompt, and tools.\n\n### 🔥 Long-Running AI Developer Workflows\nWhen you take the core four and wrap it in an agentic coding tool like Claude Code, you can create long running end-to-end AI developer workflows that run for minutes to hours with and without your oversight.\n\n### 🔥 Programmable Agentic Coding\nClaude Code is programmable - you can run it from any programming language that has terminal access. We can embed our own agents, workflows, and agentic prompts across the software development lifecycle.\n\n### 🔥 Building Systems That Build Systems\nWe need this capability of having a programmable agentic coding tool because we want to be building systems that build systems for us. We can embed our tooling across developer environments to drive real engineering outcomes.\n\n### 🔥 Lesson 1 Foundation Complete\nThis essential tactic, stop coding, and the key difference between AI coding and agentic coding will ripple throughout every lesson moving forward. Agentic coding is about building systems that build systems on our behalf.\n\n### 🔥 To Become Irreplaceable, Replace Yourself\nThe contradicting truth about what you'll learn in tactical agentic coding: To become an irreplaceable engineer, you will replace yourself. You won't see any vibe coders replicating what you'll be able to do. Agentic Engineer Master AI Coding, AI Agents, and Agentics to build 'living' software Blogs Pi Coding Agent: The Only Claude Code Competitor Top 2% Agentic Engineering The Agent Thread Framework State of AI Coding Compute Advantage Resources Home Account Tactical Agentic Coding Principled AI Coding YouTube Terms Privacy\n","numLines":91,"startLine":1,"totalLines":91}}},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CcxHwaCZfKkxM95hXEUsE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EC9x1MptttUGbYWAF4JSSd","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kvnkishore/WebstormProjects/AgenticEngineer/IndyDevDan/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5417,"cache_read_input_tokens":42433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5417},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a","uuid":"86060529-58b1-4e46-a657-b54393ac29b8","request_id":"req_011CcxHwY5p1YaAvpniQPaxx"},{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EC9x1MptttUGbYWAF4JSSd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# tac-1-hello-agentic-coding — Hello Agentic Coding\n2\t\n3\tCourse: **TAC** · order 1\n4\t\n5\t| Asset | Path |\n6\t|-------|------|\n7\t| Video | `video/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding.mp4` |\n8\t| Transcript | `transcript/` (vtt + md/txt when available) |\n9\t| Course page HTML | `metadata/course-page.html` (real AE HTML + local CSS/fonts/images) |\n10\t| Metadata JSON | `metadata/lesson.json` |\n11\t| Codebase | `codebase/` → `tac/tac-1` |\n12\t\n13\tSource: https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding/course/hello-agentic-coding\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a","uuid":"40174675-ab30-4a3f-9aee-8972a5378e9c","timestamp":"2026-07-12T14:07:06.670Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kvnkishore/WebstormProjects/AgenticEngineer/IndyDevDan/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding/README.md","content":"# tac-1-hello-agentic-coding — Hello Agentic Coding\n\nCourse: **TAC** · order 1\n\n| Asset | Path |\n|-------|------|\n| Video | `video/tac-1-hello-agentic-coding.mp4` |\n| Transcript | `transcript/` (vtt + md/txt when available) |\n| Course page HTML | `metadata/course-page.html` (real AE HTML + local CSS/fonts/images) |\n| Metadata JSON | `metadata/lesson.json` |\n| Codebase | `codebase/` → `tac/tac-1` |\n\nSource: https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding/course/hello-agentic-coding\n","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}}},{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":50,"estimated_tokens_delta":50,"uuid":"b80171d9-7875-40ee-b340-a3ac28eb6866","session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a"},{"type":"system","subtype":"thinking_tokens","estimated_tokens":160,"estimated_tokens_delta":110,"uuid":"a50db29f-b51b-4109-98c4-ff3703684138","session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a"},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CcxHxe617tGg7mESJ2dJm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12851,"cache_read_input_tokens":47850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12851},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2b29d221-2a38-404f-babf-a4bbd9f0c72a","uuid":"2b963a3c-4e9f-4aaa-b124-121529e7cc2b","request_id":"req_011CcxHxchfB96eF9oVjHAEF"},{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CcxHxe617tGg7mESJ2dJm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Transcript and notes are in. Now reading the full codebase and the VTT for timestamps