okN4AQ==&rs=AOn4CLAuvh8gUHjNid54S2RZybKMgvY3AQ", "height": 110, "width": 196, "preference": -7, "id": "31", "resolution": "196x110"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EnXKysJNz_8/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEjCPYBEIoBSFryq4qpAxUIARUAAAAAGAElAADIQj0AgKJDeAE=&rs=AOn4CLDOebr5yq7i3RraBviAIuojYU8Btw", "height": 138, "width": 246, "preference": -7, "id": "32", "resolution": "246x138"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EnXKysJNz_8/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEjCNACELwBSFryq4qpAxUIARUAAAAAGAElAADIQj0AgKJDeAE=&rs=AOn4CLAAVSxrKjLpBQF-zvhPuMdSAo0uag", "height": 188, "width": 336, "preference": -7, "id": "33", "resolution": "336x188"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EnXKysJNz_8/hqdefault.jpg", "height": 360, "width": 480, "preference": -7, "id": "34", "resolution": "480x360"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/EnXKysJNz_8/hqdefault.webp", "preference": -6, "id": "35"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EnXKysJNz_8/sddefault.jpg", "height": 480, "width": 640, "preference": -5, "id": "36", "resolution": "640x480"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/EnXKysJNz_8/sddefault.webp", "preference": -4, "id": "37"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EnXKysJNz_8/hq720.jpg", "preference": -3, "id": "38"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/EnXKysJNz_8/hq720.webp", "preference": -2, "id": "39"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EnXKysJNz_8/maxresdefault.jpg", "height": 1080, "width": 1920, "preference": -1, "id": "40", "resolution": "1920x1080"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/EnXKysJNz_8/maxresdefault.webp", "preference": 0, "id": "41"}], "thumbnail": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/EnXKysJNz_8/maxresdefault.jpg", "description": "Prompting back and forth with a single agent in 2026, will be like writing code by hand in 2025. You'll be FAR FAR BEHIND your co-workers, and the rest of the industry. \n\nEvery benchmark from the insane April stack of releases has a MAJOR FLAW. Somethings missing. In this video, we breakdown exactly what and how you can take advantage of it in your agentic engineering work. \n\n🔥 The Verifier Agent is the multi-agent coding pattern hiding in plain sight. Agents validating agents. Agent to agent communication that actually saves you time.\n\n🔥 GET THE VERIFIER AGENT\n• GET THE VERIFIER AGENT (FREE): https://github.com/disler/the-verifier-agent\n• GET THE FULL VERIFIER AGENT: https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding?y=EnXKysJNz_8\n\n🔗 RESOURCES FOR YOU\n• PI DEV: https://pi.dev/\n• CHAT GPT IMAGE 2: https://openai.com/index/introducing-chatgpt-images-2-0/\n• STRIPE BLUEPRINT AGENTS: https://youtu.be/V5A1IU8VVp4\n• MULTI-AGENT TEAMS: https://youtu.be/RairMJflUSA\n\n🚀 April 2026 hit the highest model release velocity ever - Opus 4.7, GPT 5.5, Deepseek V4, GLM 5.1, Kimi-K 2.6, the Qwen series. But model performance is no longer the bottleneck. YOU are. Your ability to extract value out of agentic systems at scale - safely - is the only thing that matters in the age of agentic engineering.\n\n🤖 In this video, IndyDevDan breaks down the verifier agent: a brutally simple two-agent multi agent orchestration pattern where Opus 4.7 builds and GPT 5.5 verifies completely unprompted. Watch a pi coding agent generate a hero image with GPT Image 2, then watch the second pi agent automatically validate every atomic claim, reject the work for violating the readability contract, and re-prompt the builder agent through a Unix socket - hands off the keyboard.\n\n🛠️ This is the future of ai coding. We're not talking about delegation. We're not talking about sub-agents. We're talking about agents validating agents - coordinated multi-agent coding where one agent watches, verifies, and only gives feedback when necessary. The verifier agent attacks the review constraint head-on. You spend tokens to save time. You template your engineering into the system prompt by force, because the harness won't let you fire one-off prompts. No vibe coding allowed.\n\n💡 Why this matters:\n- Two constraints rule agentic coding: planning and reviewing\n- The verifier crushes the review constraint with atomic claim validation\n- Built-in positive feedback loops compound with every prompt\n- Restricted bash policies lock down the most dangerous tool agents have\n- Owns your agent harness - claude code, codex, gemini, opencode all change underneath your feet\n\n🔥 Every model benchmark on the planet is making the same mistake from an engineer's perspective - they test ONE model in isolation. Real intelligence isn't GPT 5.5 OR Opus 4.7. It's GPT 5.5 AND Opus 4.7. Stack intelligence. Orchestrate intelligence. Own your pi agent harness.\n\n🌟 The two engineers of 2026: those stuck prompting back and forth, and those building systems like this verifier agent that scale far beyond ai coding. Tactical agentic coding members get the souped-up version with specialized verifier experts and the GPT Image 2 skill. Vibe coding is the floor. Agentic engineering is the ceiling no one has imagined yet.\n\nStay focused and keep building.\n\n📖 Chapters\n00:00 Aprils Insane Model Release Velocity\n01:35 The Verifier Agent\n09:40 The Two Constraints of Agentic Coding\n23:00 What's missing from Every LLM Benchmark\n25:38 Tactical Agentic Coding\n30:25 The focus for the IndyDevDan Channel\n\n#aicoding #agenticengineering #agenticcoding", "channel_id": "UC_x36zCEGilGpB1m-V4gmjg", "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC_x36zCEGilGpB1m-V4gmjg", "duration": 1971, "view_count": 31769, "age_limit": 0, "webpage_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EnXKysJNz_8", "categories": ["Science & Technology"], "tags": [], "playable_in_embed": true, "live_status": "not_live", "media_type": "video", "_format_sort_fields": ["quality", "res", "fps", "hdr:12", "source", "vcodec", "channels", "acodec", "lang", "proto"], "automatic_captions": {"ab": [{"ext": "json3", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/api/timedtext?v=EnXKysJNz_8&ei=XxpTarbAHdbeybgPhdTokAs&caps=asr&opi=112496729&xoaf=5&xowf=1&xospf=1&hl=en&ip=0.0.0.0&ipbits=0&expire=1783856335&sparams=ip%2Cipbits